EFS may assign the Playboy Commerce agreement to an acquirer of all or substantially all of its assets without the Client’s prior written consent only if, in the Client’s reasonable judgment:  

1. Key EFS management (as defined by the Client at the time of acquisition) will remain with EFS indefinitely, or any replacement management is reasonably acceptable to the Client and is no less experienced than the existing team【Chunk 1】;  
2. The acquirer can demonstrate sufficient financial resources and the intention to invest in growing the Playboy Commerce Business, including having a net‑worth at least equal to EFS’s as of the Effective Date【Chunk 2】;  
3. The assignment will not have a detrimental impact on the Playboy Commerce Business or the Client’s other businesses【Chunk 2】; and  
4. The acquirer is able to honor all financial terms of the agreement and assume all of EFS’s obligations hereunder【Chunk 2】.  

Additionally, EFS may not assign the agreement without consent to a competitor of the Client or any of the Client’s businesses【Chunk 2】.
